I love playing doppelgangers in Slash'em. That, however, does not
translate into playing doppelgangers *well* in slash'em, so I'd like
to devote a thread to cute doppelganger techniques. To start things
off,

0. Poly into nymph and get massive discounts at shops.

I love this technique because doppelgangers seem to have low natural
charisma, and nymphs have CHA 18 for obvious reasons. Unfortunately,
the nymph's *other* ability led to a YASD for a promising doppelganger
rogue:

Male Shopkeeper: "For you, hotness, only 20 for this food ration-"
Nymph/doppelganger: "poof" (teleportitis).
You teleport out of the shop, holding the food ration.
Shopkeeper: "THAT NYMPH DONE STOLE MY 20 ZORKMIDS!"
The shopkeeper wields a shotgun! The keystone kops are after you! The
watchmen want to kill you!
.
.
.
DYWYPI? Ah, isn't love a fickle thing.

1. poly into Xorn and raid vaults.
Pro: great way to explore, immunity to footrices ("you enter a
disgusting nest!" is a common message in Slash'em), lots of gems!

Con: you'd *better* have a wand or ring of polymorph or scroll of
teleportation in case you get stuck in a wall.

2. turn into a mind flayer and visit the Minetown buffet - all you can
eat (brains)!

A mind flayer is an excellent early polymorph for most doppelgangers,
since they have enormous attack power and can usually be poly'd by a
exp 6 doppelganger.

Unfortunately, I once tried this technique as a monk. Needless to say,
the monk's enforced vegetarianism conduct made this polymorph
significantly less usable. SLURP! you feel guilty. SLURP! you feel
guilty... you get the picture.

3. turn into a cockatrice to lay eggs/"stoning grenades".
The obvious downside is the -2 luck penalty for breaking your own
eggs. Like they say, the devteam thinks of everything.

4. turn into a giant and push Sokoban aside.
I believe there's a luck penalty for this, just like for every other
shortcut in Sokoban, but am not sure.



